egan failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18). I rolled the service back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted partway with an orchestrator error after us-east had moved to v2.3.0, so the rollback was re-issued and completed. Current status: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy and was not redeployed. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure during rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-incident"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it is healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy, and v2.3.1-rc was only ever in staging.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the service in a mixed state. I checked the status and re-issued the same rollback, which completed across all regions.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0002 for checkout-api, and the on-call engineer was paged. The first incident request timed out, so I retried it with an idempotency key. The service returned one incident, INC-0002, so there should be no duplicate, but it's worth confirming in the incident list.\n- **Follow-up:** v2.3.1 was not redeployed. The incident summary asks for an investigation into the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error during rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}